{
  "info": {
    "name": "Chat Application API",
    "description": "One request per real API endpoint (30 total, matching routes/api.php exactly) - no scenario duplicates. Run top to bottom inside each folder; tokens and IDs are captured automatically into collection variables as you go.\n\nSETUP:\n1. Set `base_url` (default http://localhost:8000).\n2. Run '1. Authentication' > Signup, then open storage/logs/mail.log in your project folder, copy the raw `Token:` value for that email, paste it into 'Verify Email' request's body, then run Verify Email, then Login.\n\nIMPORTANT GAP TO KNOW ABOUT: every Signup call creates a brand-new company - there is no 'join an existing company' endpoint in the spec. So to test 'Add Team Member' / 'Add Channel Member' with a second real user in the SAME company, you must: (a) run Signup again with different data (this creates User B in their own separate Company B), then (b) open MongoDB Compass and manually change that second user's `company_id` field to match User A's `company_id`, so they appear as a same-company colleague. This is a data-seeding step outside the API, not a bug - the spec has no self-service way to add a colleague to an existing company.\n\nNEW: channels support a `visibility` field (\"public\" or \"private\", default \"private\"). Public channels are visible to and self-joinable (POST /api/channels/{channelId}/join) by every member of that channel's team; private channels stay fully invite-only and hidden from non-members. See README section 7a for details.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "user_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "company_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "member_user_id",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SAME_COMPANY_USER_ID"
    },
    {
      "key": "team_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "channel_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "message_id",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Signup",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/signup",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Elon Musk\",\n  \"email\": \"elon@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"ElonMusk12\",\n  \"company_name\": \"Tesla\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Creates the user (pending verification), a new company, the default 'General Team', and the default 'Announcements' channel. No token is returned here - signup does not log you in."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify Email",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/verify-email",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"PASTE_RAW_TOKEN_FROM_storage/logs/mail.log_HERE\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "The raw verification token is never returned by any API response (only its SHA-256 hash is stored, per the spec's security rules). Open storage/logs/mail.log in your project folder and copy the 'Token:' value for this email, then paste it above."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 && json.data && json.data.token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.data.token);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', json.data.user.id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('company_id', json.data.user.company_id);",
                  "    console.log('Saved token, user_id, company_id.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"elon@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"ElonMusk12\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Requires a verified account. Saves the bearer token + user_id + company_id into collection variables automatically - every request below inherits Authorization: Bearer {{token}} from the collection."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend Verification",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/resend-verification",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"elon@example.com\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Only useful BEFORE verifying (e.g. if the original token expired). Issues a new token and invalidates the old one - if you run this, re-copy the token from mail.log before calling Verify Email again."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify Email (via emailed link)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/verify-email?token=PASTE_RAW_TOKEN_HERE",
            "description": "Same behavior as the POST version above, exposed as GET so the link inside the actual verification email is clickable in a browser."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/logout",
            "description": "Revokes {{token}} server-side. Run this LAST - every request after this will correctly start failing with 401 until you log in again."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. User & Company",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Authenticated User (Me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/me"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Company",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/company"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Company Users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/company/users",
            "description": "Once you've manually migrated a second user's company_id in Compass (see collection description), you'll see them here - copy their id into the member_user_id variable to use in the Teams/Channels folders below."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Teams",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Team",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.team) { pm.collectionVariables.set('team_id', json.data.team.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Engineering\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Teams",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Team",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Team",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Engineering Team\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add Team Member",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}/members",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"{{member_user_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Requires member_user_id to be a real user in the SAME company (see collection description for how to get one)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Team Members",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}/members"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Remove Team Member",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}/members/{{member_user_id}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Channels",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Channel",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.channel) { pm.collectionVariables.set('channel_id', json.data.channel.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}/channels",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"backend-api\",\n  \"visibility\": \"public\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "visibility is optional (\"public\" or \"private\", defaults to \"private\"). Public channels are visible to and self-joinable by every team member; private channels stay invite-only."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Channels",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}/channels"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Channel",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Channel",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"backend-api-v2\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add Channel Member",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}/members",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"{{member_user_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Requires member_user_id to already be a member of this channel's TEAM (run 'Add Team Member' first)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Join Channel",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}/join",
            "description": "Self-join a PUBLIC channel - works for any team member without needing an existing member to add them first. Returns 403 if the channel is private, or 409 if you're already a member."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Channel Members",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}/members"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Remove Channel Member",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}/members/{{member_user_id}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Messages",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send Message",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.message) { pm.collectionVariables.set('message_id', json.data.message.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}/messages",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Hello team!\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Messages",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}/messages?limit=50&skip=0"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Message",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/messages/{{message_id}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Message",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/messages/{{message_id}}",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Hello team! (edited)\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Message",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/messages/{{message_id}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Cleanup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Delete Channel",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/channels/{{channel_id}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Team",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/teams/{{team_id}}",
            "description": "Deleting a team cascades and deletes any channels still inside it - run this AFTER the Messages folder, not before."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}